  "content": {
    "title": "Chipotle offering BOGO burritos (and more) today. How to get",
    "text": "Updated March 13, 2026, 2:22 p.m. ETFriday the 13th may get a bad reputation, but at least you can get a free burrito on the day.Chipotle Mexican Grill is offering a buy-one-get-one-free deal for any menu item during a \"flash\" one-hour sale on Friday, March 13, according to a release from the company. But there's a catch.Fans need to show up in the restaurant with any tattoo − whether it's permanent ink, a temporary tatoo or a drawn-on design − to cash in on the promotion.The promotion will take place from 3 to 4 p.m. local time across the U.S. The BOGO offer is limited to five free menu items per check. Each free item requires the purchase of an entrée item of equal or greater value and may be collected only by a tattoo-wearing customer, the terms of the deal state.The idea for the promotion is a play on a tattoo shop tradition. On Friday the 13th, tattoo shops often drop \"flash sheets,\" or small, pre-designed tattoos to commemorate the day, the release reads. What do tattoos have to do with Chipotle? Well, Chipotle is giving a cheeky nod to a bunch of memes on the internet about people being \"tatted like a Chipotle bag.\" Chipotle's take-out bags are heavily decorated with thin-lined, black doodles.Chipotle restaurant locationsTo find your nearest Chipotle, use the website's store locator. You can also find a location near you via the list of Chipotle locations in Ohio and the list of Chipotle locations in Kentucky.",
